# evidence-signing.yml — recorder-side signing-mode binding for the evidence
# store (HP-1; framework/evidence/signing.py resolves this file at
# <store_root>/../../config/evidence-signing.yml, which for the production
# store instance/evidence/v1 is THIS directory). Copy to evidence-signing.yml
# and uncomment ONLY at the deploy ceremony.
#
# THE DARK DEFAULT IS ABSENCE, NOT `mode: local`: with no file here the
# recorder loads/creates the store's own .signing-key and signs in-process,
# byte-identical to the pre-seam recorder. Scratch and test stores resolve
# this path to a location that does not exist, so they are local-mode and
# hermetic by construction.
#
# A file that is present but does not declare `mode: broker` is still local
# mode. A file that declares broker mode with a dead or refusing socket is a
# typed, FAIL-CLOSED evidence error — never a silent local fallback (a
# fallback would be the downgrade attack: kill the daemon, forge locally).
#
# THREAT HONESTY: HP-1 raises the evidence-forgery bar from same-OS-user to
# root. Root can still forge events, anchors, watermarks, the broker's
# request log, and the key itself; a compromise of the broker user is a key
# compromise. Those residuals are accepted and stated — external anchoring
# (evidence-anchor) exists for after-the-fact detection. Before the ceremony
# this file does not exist and cannot be immutability-locked (locks skip
# absent paths): a same-user writer creating a bogus one buys evidence-plane
# DENIAL (loud, fail-closed) or a redirect to an attacker socket — which
# grants nothing beyond the same-user forgery power that already exists
# without HP-1.
#
# THE REAL FILE IS BORN AT THE DEPLOY CEREMONY (Captain sudo,
# docs/runbooks/evidence-signing-broker.md), root-owned, and added to the
# germline lock set via the immutable-core pending: mechanism in the same
# ceremony. Only this .example ships.

# Signing mode: `broker` routes every recorder signature through the
# out-of-process key holder (framework/evidence_signing_broker.py). Any
# other value — or the key being absent — is local mode.
#mode: broker

# Unix socket served by the evidence-signing-broker daemon (~ expands).
# Required in broker mode; broker mode without a socket is a typed refusal.
#socket: /var/run/cabinet/evidence-signing.sock

# Optional CLAIMED identity sent with every request. The broker checks the
# claim against its kernel-attested peer-uid map and refuses a mismatch —
# the claim can narrow, never widen.
#identity: officer-core
